WEBVTT

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:02.373
and billing is not so
exciting, or signing a lease,

00:07:02.397 --> 00:07:05.689
so I was really excited about the idea
of stripping away all the stuff

00:07:05.713 --> 00:07:07.299
that was not their core activity,

00:07:07.323 --> 00:07:09.091
and I was pretty charged up with that

00:07:09.115 --> 00:07:11.099
and that's how I interpreted the mission.

00:07:11.123 --> 00:07:12.321
AG: Got it.

00:07:12.345 --> 00:07:15.455
That could almost be the slogan
for this podcast that I host.

00:07:15.479 --> 00:07:17.882
(Laughter)

00:07:17.906 --> 00:07:20.279
So that, if you frame
the mission that way,

00:07:20.303 --> 00:07:23.400
I could even imagine myself
getting excited about it.

00:07:23.424 --> 00:07:26.115
I'm curious about how the mission
got communicated.

00:07:26.139 --> 00:07:29.066
What were the major ways
that the mission was brought to life?